AB  - This study proposes an improved You Only Look Once version 8 (YOLOv8) method for real-time bolt loosening detection, integrating improved target detection with precise bolt angle estimation. The approach employs a Mobile Vision Transformer (MobileViT) backbone to improve both local and global feature extraction while incorporating a large separable kernel attention module into the spatial pyramid pooling fast. In addition, content-aware reassembly features upsampling and a bi-directional feature pyramid network are used for effective multi-scale feature fusion, and a dedicated small-target detection layer enhances detection of small bolts. For angle estimation, the system leverages the scale-invariant feature transform (SIFT) for robust keypoint detection, fast library for approximate nearest neighbors (FLANN) for rapid feature matching, and random sample consensus (RANSAC) for outlier rejection, ensuring high-precision rotation estimation. An efficient intersection over union (IoU) loss function further refines bounding box regression. Extensive experiments conducted on a self-constructed dataset demonstrate that the improved model attains mean average precision (mAP) values of mAP@50 95.9 % and mAP@95 81.1 %, respectively, while maintaining real-time performance and robustness. Notably, the method reliably detects bolt rotation angles with integer-level precision, which aligns with practical measurement capabilities where sub-degree resolution is generally unattainable. Overall, the proposed system provides a reliable solution for bolt loosening detection with promising potential for large-scale industrial applications. These results indicate significant improvements in operational efficiency and detection reliability in practical applications.
