AB  - Aiming at the problems of lack of theoretical guidance in structural design and limited feature extraction capability in traditional echo state network (ESN) for temporal modeling, this paper proposes an I Ching-based multi-reservoir ESN (IC-MRESN). The model employs a taiji reservoir for global regulation to capture long-term dependencies, a five-elements reservoir for local dynamic feature enhancement based on mutual generation and restriction relationships, and an eight diagrams reservoir for high-level feature decomposition and abstraction, thereby forming a synergistic and efficient hierarchical feature extraction mechanism. Adaptive optimization of information flow is achieved through dynamic interactions driven by energy intensity and state correlations among the reservoirs. Theoretical analysis demonstrates that the architecture enables efficient feature compression and transmission based on the information bottleneck principle, while exhibiting superior function approximation capability with an ultra-compact neuron scale. Finally, experimental validation on real-world energy data shows that the model outperforms other comparative models in prediction accuracy, generalization ability, and noise resistance under a simplified network topology.
