AB  - IoT (Internet of Things) is an interconnected network, wherein, the objects within the network collect and transfer data through wireless network. MQTT (Message Queuing Telemetry Transport) has become renowned in IoT owing to its efficacy, and simplicity. MQTT is a light-weight IoT communication protocol, holding a publisher subscriber message model. It permits for data transfer through devices with intricateness as in conventional MQTT models, the publisher-client and the subscriber-client can be linked only to a broker, thereby perform data exchange on a particular topic. Further, formerly published data is broadcasted to all the brokers within the dispersed network, leading to broker crashing down. Considering this issue, the present study proposes a topic re-routing mechanism in IoT based SDN environment, wherein, the multi-broker network is managed via re-routing to the clients linked with crashed MQTT brokers for accomplishing an uninterrupted data exchange with high availability and scalability. In this case, G-G (Greedy Genetic algorithm) is used for improving load balancing and energy consumption rate through the determination of the fitness value. Greedy approach can assist the selection process of the genetic approach. Rather than choosing individuals in random way, the greedy method could be used for prioritizing individuals that possess potential for enhancement. This could assist in diversity maintenance in population while concentrating on reliable solutions. The overall performance rate of the proposed work is evaluated through comparison with traditional works with regard to metrics for uncovering the efficiency of the proposed model. Outcomes unveiled the better performance of the proposed system. The advantages of the proposed algorithm include enhanced fault tolerance due to dynamic topic re-routing, improved load balancing which prevents broker overload, and reduced energy consumption resulting from optimized resource allocation. Additionally, the integration of the greedy approach accelerates convergence, leading to faster and more reliable optimization results. The model's general applicability spans diverse IoT environments such as smart cities, industrial automation, and healthcare systems where large-scale, dynamic, and reliable communication is critical. By ensuring uninterrupted data flow and scalability, this approach can effectively support complex IoT deployments requiring high availability and efficient network management.
