AB  - Cotton leaf diseases greatly impact India's textile, food, pharmaceutical, and export sectors. They lower the combined share of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) from about 2 to 2.3 % down to 1.3–1.7 % because of yield losses of 30–35 %. Manual detection is likely to have human errors. Traditional deep learning models also have drawbacks like small datasets, variations in scale, irregular lesion shapes, and missing fine details. This research presents an improved stacked EnsembleNet framework that combines three specialized models. The first is an Efficient Hierarchical Network for extracting features at multi-scale levels. The second is an Efficient Shape Convolutional Neural Network that captures small structural and morphological differences. The third is an Efficient Non-Local Convolutional Neural Network that focuses on context-aware learning. The framework is tested using standard performance metrics. The proposed model acquired an accuracy of 97.80 and the Cohen's kappa of 0.9748, confirming that the model is strong and reliable for classifying diseases. The research shows the importance of the suggested system in accurately identifying cotton leaf diseases from gathered datasets. This establishes a basis for future smart disease management systems.
